Speaking for the majority of the Constitution Bench,
Gajendra gadkar, J. observed as under: (AIR pp. 479-80, para 7) "7. ... A writ of certiorari can be issued for correcting errors of jurisdiction committed by inferior courts or tribunals;
these are cases where orders are passed by inferior courts or tribunals without jurisdiction, or is in excess of it, or as a result of failure to exercise jurisdiction.
